# Follow-on: the next confirmed reset (back to Grocery) resolved its clear module from the cart's first item module (the mismatched Grocery item) and sent DELETE cart/remove moduleId='1' -> the Pharmacy rows 1086/1087 SURVIVED the confirmed reset server-side (orphans; removed by QA from the copy DB afterwards):
00:20:35.135 DELETE /api/v1/customer/cart/remove q= moduleId='1' zoneId=None -> 200 [93ms] rows=[]
#   DB after: 1088 cart_mod 1 Zqx Rice | 1086 cart_mod 3 Zqx Rice Two (item mod 1) q2 | 1087 cart_mod 3 Zqx Pill
# Client side: [WARN] 'pending add dropped: reason=module_mismatch item_id=990008 row_module_id=1 active_module_id=3' -> local basket drops the row while the server keeps it (client/server divergence until the next reload).
# Likely mechanism (read, not proven): the stepper '+' re-schedules the item's debounce (new Timer, not identical to the one in syncsAtClear), so the success-path identity cancel misses it; it is held, then fired after success; _syncItem captures _clearedEpoch at its own start (already post-increment), and by then the module header is the new one.
